:: Temple Library
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "temple">><<temple_effects>><<effects>>

<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
    The library is empty and silent.
<<else>>
    <<Monks_and_Nuns>> study in the library, looking for books in the vast shelves or reading at the various tables.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if isPlayerNonparasitePregnancyEnding() and !$possessed>>
	<<pregnancyPassout "temple">>
<<elseif $stress gte $stressmax>>
	<<passouttemple>>
<<elseif $exposed gte 1>>
    You creep around the library, concealing your nudity behind a column of gargoyles whenever you hear the shuffle of feet.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Cloister (0:01)|Temple Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
    <br>
<<else>>
    <<projectoptions>>
    <br><br>
    <<if !$worn.handheld.name.includes("Book of Scripture")>>
        <span class="blue">You can't study without your Book of Scripture</span>
    <<else>>
        <<link [[Study Book of Scripture (0:30)|Temple Library Study]]>><<pass 30>><<grace 2>><</link>><<ggrace>>
    <</if>>
    <br><br>
     <<link [[Cloister (0:01)|Temple Cloister]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
    <br>   
<</if>>

:: Temple Library Study
/*Currently has no danger elements*/
<<if $rng gte 75>> /*Gives Willpower or Awareness based on current awareness*/
    You open your Book up to a random page and find a record of a sermon.
    <br><br>
    /*Need to write a sermon and put it here, gonna need to figure out more about what a sermon of the temple would contain
      Sermon should start about the dangers of the world (your adversary the devil walks about like a roaring lion type vibe)
      and then transition to something meant to empower those in the faith of their ability to resist said evils.
      If someone's reading this and feels like they can write a bulletpoint of things I feel pretty confident in writting a sermon I just don't know what the content should be.
    */
    <<if $awareness gte 400>>
        The sermon makes you feel empowered. <<gwillpower>><<willpower 2>>
    <<else>>
        The sermon feels enlightening, about the dangers of the world and how to protect yourself from them. <<gawareness>><<awareness 6>>
    <</if>>
<<elseif $rng gte 50>> /*Mimics finding a scroll in the quarters, giving you either awareness or history*/
    As you study you begin reading an account of the founding of a temple.
    <br><br>
    <<if $rng gte 80>>
        The account tells of the battles and trials faced by the clergy. On this passage the story focuses on virtous <<monks_and_nuns>> and their triumph. When you check the cross references, though, you see writtings about their failures and the unholliness of the surrounding people.
        <<gawareness>><<awareness 6>>
    <<else>>
        It's a histroical account of the founding more than a story. It lists the names of the founders, their ages, and their achivements. Then how the temple was constructed, where the materials were taken from and what they were, the measurements of different rooms and decorative embellishments.
        <br><br>
        You're not sure how much of it is embellished, but when cross checking it to a history book you find from the shelves the recording of it's construction matches.
        <<historyskill>><<ghistory>>
    <</if>>
<<else>> /*Gives English*/
    You read through the scriptures, occasional adding a notation in the margins.
    <<englishskill>> <<genglish>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

